/A 3150 0 R
/Alt (A six panel forest plot shows consensus beta values for various microbial species across different caries related phenotypes. The vertical axis lists numerous species names, with some highlighted in a different colour. The horizontal axis is labelled Consensus beta plus or minus 1.96 SE, with tick marks from 0 to 4. The six panels are labelled D0, D1, D2, D3, DMFS, and FS. Panel D0 shows mostly positive beta values for species like Catonella morbi and Fusobacterium periodonticum, indicated by filled circular markers with error bars. Panel D1 is mostly empty, with only a few markers near zero. Panel D2 shows several markers clustered around zero, with one filled marker for Lactobacillus gasseri. Panel D3 shows positive beta values for species like Actinomyces radicidentis and Lactobacillus crispatus, with some filled and some unfilled markers. Panel DMFS shows positive beta values for many species, including Bifidobacterium longum and Streptococcus mutans, with a mix of filled and unfilled markers. Panel FS also shows positive beta values for several species, such as Kingella oralis and Streptococcus sobrinus, with mostly unfilled markers. Filled markers indicate concordant significant associations in both MET and ONT analyses, while unfilled markers indicate significance in only one platform.)
/ID (OAJKHE+)
/K 0
/P 533 0 R
/Pg 19 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
