/A 3155 0 R
/Alt (A two panel figure displays species prevalence and mean relative abundance across four cohorts: MODS MET, MODS ONT, STAGE, and SMAC. Panel A shows species prevalence as a percentage on the horizontal axis, with values ranging from 0 to 100 for MODS MET and MODS ONT, 0 to 10 for STAGE, and 0 to 50 for SMAC. Ten species are listed on the vertical axis: Lactobacillus crispatus, Lactobacillus gasseri, Lactobacillus ultunensis, Ligilactobacillus salivarius, Limosilactobacillus fermentum, Limosilactobacillus vaginalis, Olsenella profusa, Parascardovia denticolens, Streptococcus mutans, and Streptococcus sobrinus. Bars represent point estimates with horizontal whiskers for 95 percent confidence intervals. Streptococcus mutans shows the highest prevalence in MODS MET, MODS ONT, and STAGE, while Limosilactobacillus fermentum is highest in SMAC. Panel B shows mean relative abundance as a percentage on the horizontal axis, with values ranging from 0 to 0.25 for MODS MET and MODS ONT, 0 to 0.020 for STAGE, and 0 to 0.12 for SMAC. The same ten species are listed on the vertical axis. Bars represent point estimates with horizontal whiskers for bootstrap 95 percent confidence intervals. Limosilactobacillus fermentum shows the highest mean relative abundance in MODS MET, while Streptococcus mutans is highest in STAGE and SMAC.)
/ID (LMGDKZ+)
/K 0
/P 551 0 R
/Pg 20 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
